---
title: Authentication — rotating refresh tokens and reuse detection
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor C as Customer
    participant W as Next.js
    participant A as NestJS API
    participant D as PostgreSQL

    rect rgb(232, 237, 244)
    Note over C,D: Registration
    C->>W: email, password, name
    W->>A: POST /auth/register
    A->>A: argon2id hash (never store the password)
    A->>D: INSERT user (role CUSTOMER)
    A->>D: INSERT refresh_token (sha256 hash only)
    A-->>W: Set-Cookie sr_access (15 min) + sr_refresh (30 days)
    Note right of W: httpOnly, SameSite=Lax.<br/>XSS cannot read either cookie.
    end

    rect rgb(220, 232, 220)
    Note over C,D: Normal use
    C->>W: Open account page
    W->>A: GET /auth/me (cookie attached automatically)
    A->>A: Verify access JWT
    A-->>W: user profile
    end

    rect rgb(253, 246, 227)
    Note over C,D: Access token expires after 15 minutes
    W->>A: POST /auth/refresh
    A->>D: Look up sha256(presented token)
    alt Token valid and unspent
        A->>D: Mark old token revoked
        A->>D: INSERT replacement token
        A-->>W: new cookie pair
    else Token already spent — it leaked
        A->>D: Revoke EVERY session for that user
        A-->>W: 401 — sign in again
        Note right of A: One replay ends all sessions,<br/>not just the stolen one.
    end
    end

    rect rgb(239, 228, 240)
    Note over C,D: Forgotten password
    C->>W: Enter email address
    W->>A: POST /auth/forgot-password
    A->>D: Store single-use token, one hour expiry
    A-->>W: 202 — identical response whether or not the account exists
    Note right of A: No account enumeration
    C->>W: Open emailed link, choose new password
    W->>A: POST /auth/reset-password
    A->>D: Update hash, mark token used, revoke all sessions
    end
